in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/spectral/portal

# @mirror/spectral/portal/stream — the bidirectional eigenvalue stream
# at the mirror altitude. Three actions; fourth wire stage of the
# four-stage portal protocol.
#
# THE T18 SUB-SPECIES under @mirror/spectral/portal. Lifts the boot-
# altitude `@spectral/portal/stream` declaration to the mirror altitude.
# Three action signatures preserved verbatim from the boot floor;
# bodies stay at the boot altitude per the transitional-placeholder
# discipline until the bounded-iteration substrate gap closes.
#
# === The eigenvalue-stream wire format ===
#
# Per `boot/std/spectral/portal/stream.mirror`: each value on the wire
# is 8 bytes IEEE-754 big-endian double. **Not tokens. Not bytes.
# Eigenvalues.** Each tick of the actor gen_prism reads one value,
# applies its tick map, writes one value back. The stream IS the
# gen_prism's ancestor chain made visible over the wire.
#
# This species's `read_value` / `write_value` actions ARE the wire-
# altitude realisations of the parent species's `project_eigenvalue`
# focus operation: `read_value` reads one f64 in (one scalar eigenvalue
# off the wire); `write_value` writes one f64 out. The parent's
# beam-level projection composes these per-tick wire operations into
# the substrate-typed beam<f64> the consumer pulls.
#
# Per the 26th-instance recognition (docs/insights/2026-06-08-portal-
# eigenvalue-stream-gen-prism.md §"The portal-as-gen_prism collapse"):
# each `shift(oid, observation)` the upstream gen_prism emits projects
# through `read_value` / `write_value` to its scalar summary. The
# substrate's typed-capability primitive (`shift(oid, T)`) flows over
# the wire as eigenvalues without re-serialising the typed-capability
# itself — the OID-bytes-typed shift stays implicit; the scalar
# summary is what crosses the boundary.
#
# === The substrate gap ===
#
# `stream(c, gp, budget)` needs a structural loop / recursion primitive
# that the substrate at this altitude does not expose. Per the boot
# floor's natural composition (lines 50-58 of the boot version):
#
#   while budget > 0 and not autopoietic_settled(gp):
#     read_value(c)
#       |> message_of_value
#       |> @mirror/runtime/gen_prism.tick(gp.head, _)
#       |> advance_gp
#       |> emit_observation
#       |> write_value(c, _)
#
# The bounded-iteration primitive lands with the Scheduler Tower
# (docs/specs/scheduler-tower.md) and the @epistemologic/property/halts
# disjunction. Until then, `stream`'s body stays `\` at both altitudes;
# the substrate contract is intact (in, out, budget, gen_prism advance);
# only the loop body is parked. Halts is structurally satisfied by the
# disjunction (autopoietic settlement OR budget exhaustion).
#
# Per [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] + the T16
# transitional placeholder pattern: the boot floor stays authoritative
# for the wire bodies; this species declares the mirror-altitude typed
# surface so consumers compose at the family altitude rather than at
# the boot altitude.
#
# Spec context: docs/insights/2026-06-08-portal-eigenvalue-stream-
#               gen-prism.md (the 26th-instance recognition; the
#               substrate state never serialises to bytes between
#               processes; the stream IS the wire format),
#               docs/specs/scheduler-tower.md (the bounded-iteration
#               primitive that closes stream's body),
#               boot/std/spectral/portal/stream.mirror (the boot
#               floor; verbatim action signatures).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Substrate recognitions: [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (26th instance; read_value IS the per-tick
#                      eigenvalue projection at the wire altitude).
# Related shards: mirror/spectral/portal.mirror (the parent species;
#                 declares project_eigenvalue as the beam-level
#                 projection these per-tick read/write actions
#                 compose into),
#                 boot/std/spectral/portal/stream.mirror (the floor
#                 declaration; retained as transitional placeholder),
#                 mirror/spectral/portal/handshake.mirror (the
#                 sibling; first wire stage),
#                 mirror/spectral/portal/codec.mirror (the sibling;
#                 second wire stage).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/spectral/portal/stream.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/spectral/portal/stream` as a sub-species under
# `@mirror/spectral/portal`.

prism @mirror/spectral/portal/stream {
  focus stream
  project stream
  split stream
  shift stream
  settle stream
}

# === read_value — read one f64 observation from the wire ===
#
# Reads 8 bytes from the connection, interprets as IEEE-754
# big-endian double. The per-tick realisation of the parent species's
# project_eigenvalue focus operation.
read_value(c: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# === write_value — write one f64 observation to the wire ===
#
# Serialises an IEEE-754 double as 8 big-endian bytes; writes to the
# connection. Symmetric to read_value at the per-tick altitude.
write_value(c: ref, v: f64) -> imperfect { \ }

# === stream — drive the actor's tick loop over the open portal ===
#
# Runs the bidirectional stream until either the actor's tick map
# reaches a Lawvere fixed point (autopoietic settlement) or the
# budget exhausts. Body stays `\` pending the bounded-iteration
# primitive (per the Scheduler Tower spec).
stream(c: ref, gp: ref, budget: u64) -> imperfect { \ }

out @mirror/spectral/portal/stream
out read_value
out write_value
out stream
